nodecode-kimi-code-delegate is a rewrite of s-a-s-k-i-a's s-a-s-k-i-a/hermes-kimi-code:

  https://github.com/s-a-s-k-i-a/hermes-kimi-code
  commit 72c741cc166ec1db2aec4cd5316f7b7281a74b40
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Saskia Teichmann (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the read-only ACP delegate itself, in Common Lisp. The JSON-RPC
dialogue the CLI is driven through - initialize, authenticate against the
CLI's own login, session/new, the model and thinking config options, one
prompt whose streamed text is the answer - with the same protocol version
check, the same identity check on the agent, the same `reject_once' answer
to a permission request, the same errors for filesystem and terminal
requests, the same size limits, the same bounded redaction of child output,
and the same environment allowlist, so an unrelated key of the harness never
reaches the CLI. The tool keeps the original's arguments (prompt, model,
thinking) and its JSON answer; the doctor the plugin exposed as
`hermes kimi-code doctor' is the /kimi-code command.

Left out: the Python plugin's packaging and CLI registration, and its
`config.yaml' under `plugins.entries.kimi-code-delegate' - a cell reads its
own section of ~/.nodecode/config.jsonc instead. The original's
`command_is_available' gate (which hides the tool when the CLI is missing)
has no counterpart: the tool is registered and refuses with what to do. The
fallback to the CLI's own ~/.kimi-code/bin/kimi is kept; every other
behaviour is the original's.
